==Swedish==
[[File:Senior Airman Benton Pohlman fires an M4 carbine rifle (34135723246).jpg|thumb|300px|en man '''som skjuter''' med en automatkarbin [a man '''shooting''' with an assault rifle / [more idiomatically] a man '''firing''' an assault rifle (see the usage notes below)] ({{senseno|sv|fire}})]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|skiūta}}, from {{der|sv|non|skjóta}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*skeutaną}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*(s)kewd-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/²ɧʉːta/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-skjuta.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|sv|²ʉːta|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|skjuter|sköt|skjutit|skjut}}

# {{senseid|sv|fire}} to [[shoot]] ((a projectile with) a weapon), {{q|often, idiomatically – see the usage notes below}} to [[fire]] ((a projectile with) a weapon)
#: {{synonyms|sv|avfyra|t=fire}}
#: {{ux|sv|Det är inte bara att '''skjuta''', du måste träffa också|You can't just '''shoot''', you have to hit too}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''skjuta''' på en {{l|sv|måltavla}}|'''shoot''' at a target}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Skjut''' mot basen!|'''Fire''' at the base!|footer=''Avfyra'' sounds too technical here in Swedish.}}
#: {{ux|sv|Hon '''sköt''' mot mig|She '''fired''' at me|footer=Ditto here.}}
# to [[shoot]] (hit with a projectile fired from a weapon)
#: {{ux|sv|Han blev '''skjuten''' i armen|He was '''shot''' in the arm}}
# {{lb|sv|usually|sports}} to [[shoot]], to [[fire]] (send off (a ball, puck, or the like) with force)
#: {{ux|sv|Han '''sköt''' bollen i mål!|He '''shot''' the ball into the goal!}}
# {{lb|sv|usually with a particle}} to [[shoot]] (move swiftly (and suddenly) (like a projectile))
## {{lb|sv|idiomatic|in "skjuta i höjden"}} to [[skyrocket]], to [[shoot up]]
##: {{syn|sv|skena|rusa}}
##: {{ux|sv|Börsen '''sköt i höjden'''|The stock market '''skyrocketed'''|lit=The stock market '''shot into the height/altitude'''}}
## {{lb|sv|with {{m|sv|ut||out}}}} to [[eject]]; to [[jettison]] (from something, with force)
##: {{ux|sv|Piloten '''sköt ut sig''' ur planet|The pilot '''ejected''' from the plane|lit=The pilot '''shot himself out''' out of the plane}}
# {{lb|sv|often with {{m|sv|out||out}}}} to [[project]] (in a more or less dramatic(-sounding) fashion – like "shoot (out, etc.)," but for something static); to [[jut]], to [[protrude]], etc.
#: {{syn|sv|sträcka|alt1=sträcka sig|sticka ut|q2=stick out}}
#: {{ux|sv|en landtunga '''som skjuter ut''' i havet|a tongue of land '''jutting out''' [that shoots out] into the sea}}
#: {{ux|sv|en {{l|sv|klippa}} '''som skjuter upp ur''' havet|a rock '''jutting out of''' [that shoots out out of] the sea}}
#: {{ux|sv|en haka som '''skjuter ut'''|a chin that '''juts out''' [shoots out]}}
#: {{ux|sv|Hon snubblade på en gren som '''sköt ut''' från buskaget|She tripped on a branch that '''was protruding''' [shot out] from the bushes}}
# to [[push]], to [[shove]] (something, moving it)
#: {{ux|sv|Hon '''sköt''' lådan framför sig|She '''pushed''' the box in front of her}}
# {{senseid|sv|postpone}} {{lb|sv|usually with {{m|sv|på}} – see also {{m|sv|skjuta upp}}}} to [[push back]], to [[postpone]] (move to later)
#: {{synonyms|sv|senarelägga}}
#: {{ux|sv|Vi får '''skjuta på''' mötet till onsdag|We'll have to '''push''' the meeting '''back''' to Wednesday / We'll have to '''reschedule''' the meeting for Wednesday}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag tycker vi '''skjuter''' på schemat 30 minuter|I think we should '''push''' the schedule '''back''' by 30 minutes}}
## {{lb|sv|idiomatic|in "skjuta på framtiden"}} to [[postpone]]
##: {{syn|sv|skjuta upp}}
# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to [[scan]] (a barcode or similar)
#: {{synonyms|sv|skanna|läsa|alt2=läsa av}}
#: {{ux|sv|Glöm inte att '''skjuta''' mjölken|Don't forget to '''scan''' the milk}}
# {{lb|sv|slang|usually|transitive}} to [[shoot up]], to [[shoot]] (inject oneself with a syringe (with a recreational drug, especially heroin))
#: {{syn|sv|injicera|q=inject}}
#: {{ux|sv|En väktare såg henne '''skjuta heroin'''|A security guard saw her '''shooting up (heroin)'''}}

====Usage notes====
Compared to English, Swedish has a relatively stronger preference for {{m-self|sv|skjuta||shoot}} as opposed to {{m|sv|avfyra||fire}} for firing (projectiles from) a weapon. ''Avfyra'' sounds slightly more technical in Swedish, like a bit more towards {{m|en|discharge}}.

